# Comment on the Jira ticket when you open a PR

When a pull request is tied to a Jira issue, post a comment on that issue after the PR URL exists. Do not invent a key.

A PR is related if the user cited a key (`PROG-54`, `NOP-13`), the branch or commits contain one, or the work implements a ticket from this chat.

## Comment contents

Use the Jira comment API (Atlassian MCP `addCommentToJiraIssue` or equivalent). Include:

1. The GitHub PR URL
2. What changed — concrete behavior, 1–3 bullets (not a file list)
3. How to verify — exact command when there is one

```markdown
PR: https://github.com/<org>/<repo>/pull/7

- Qty=2 on BP_20_WSP asserts 19 without-discount (replaces the tautology)
- Golden GetFinalPriceAsync fixtures; (float) attribute-adjustment locked at 13.33433

Verify: `dotnet test src/Tests/Nop.Tests/Nop.Tests.csproj --filter FullyQualifiedName~PriceCalculationServiceTests`
```

Do not paste the issue description, customer data, secrets, or PAN.

## When to comment

- After `create_pr` / `gh pr create` succeeds — not before the URL exists
- If this PR already has a comment on the ticket, update that comment instead of posting a second one
- Skip when there is no ticket. Do not add a placeholder comment

Title/body still follow `.cursor/rules/jira-pr-links.mdc` when that file is present (`[KEY]` prefix and browse link). This rule is the ticket-side comment, not a substitute for that.
